response:
 [sigh] You’re right. I’ve been trailing you long enough. I’ve got my own research to get back to—those old Nord ruins won’t map themselves.

Good luck out there, Aldo. And if you ever need a steady hand with a torch or a lockpick, you know where to find me in Winterhold.

ACTION: Companionship PARAMS: {"intent": "Elin stops accompanying Aldo and parts ways peacefully."}

[say]Good, I knew you had the spine for it. The ledger’s in a ruined watchtower east of here, just past the old bridge over the White River. It’s not a pretty spot—bandits have been squatting there for weeks. You’ll want to go in quiet, or go in loud, but either way, don’t let them sell it before you get there.

[say]Once you have it, bring it straight back to me. I’ll be here at the inn, and I’ll make it worth your while. And if the bandits give you trouble… well, the Jarl’s guards don’t patrol that far out, so don’t expect any help.

